From d69d48d89f751b9d7f34b938382446ff4c4065a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 21:59:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] devices: export the client inventory; dashboard: make
 Security Posture rows links

DEVICES - export name / MAC / IP as CSV, JSON or HTML.
Built entirely in the browser from D.devices, which action=status has already
delivered: no CGI action, no new mime row, nothing added to httpd. There is no
outbound file-serving path in httpd to reuse in any case - every
Content-Disposition in web.c is INBOUND multipart upload parsing - so a
server-side download would have meant new plumbing for data the page is already
holding.

The name follows what the table shows: d.name (custom_clientlist, the naming
master) then the DHCP hostname. Exporting the raw hostname instead would make
the file disagree with the UI for exactly the devices the operator bothered to
rename. CSV quotes per RFC 4180; JSON and HTML carry the model and a timestamp
so an old file is identifiable later. Exports EVERY device rather than the
filtered view - this is an inventory, and a filter left set from an earlier
glance silently truncating it is what makes an export untrustworthy.

A caution sits under the button: unlike reaper_diag, which sanitizes and keeps a
withheld-items ledger precisely because raw dumps are unsafe to share, this file
is deliberately unsanitized - real names and addresses are the point - so it is
not safe to post in a forum or attach to a bug report.

DASHBOARD - every Security Posture row now takes you to the page that owns the
setting it reports. The rows stated a fact and left the operator to work out
which page could change it. All 14 wired; the two firewall rows deep-link to the
tab that owns them (Reaper_Firewall.asp?t=general, which initTab() already
supports) rather than dropping the user on Status to hunt - the ask was the page
AND the view.

The dashboard is top-level rather than framed (standing rule 39), so navigation
is location.href to the shell with the page in the hash, the same form this
page's own rail links already use. One delegated listener rather than 14
handlers, so a row added later needs only the attribute; tabindex/role are set
from JS so a row that loses its data-go stops being focusable automatically. The
hover/focus affordance is bound to [data-go], not .srow, so a row without a
destination never looks clickable.

RDEV_88..90 seeded English into all 25 packs, lockstep at 6552.

Verified without a build: 250 inline script blocks across six reaper pages parse
under node in all 25 languages, 0 unresolved tokens; reaper_langcheck 0 breakers;
every id the new JS touches exists; all 14 data-go targets resolve to pages that
exist (MLO.asp via the SDN sysdep overlay); ASCII-clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
